{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "For U1: SetXXX functions will replace existing values (override) instead of erroring; for slices (e.g., AnchorPeers), we will check for duplicates and not add if already present, but replace if desired by consumer; careful to avoid breaking existing API contracts.",
    "For U2: Rename Base() to BaseConfig() and Updated() to UpdatedConfig() for clarity; update all references and GoDoc.",
    "For U3: Introduce intermediary wrapper types (e.g., Application, Org) that expose getters/setters, allowing chaining like c.Application().Org(orgName).AddAnchorPeer(); wrap ConfigGroup proto to avoid breaking internal logic.",
    "For U4/U5: Create new packages 'orderer' and 'membership' under configtx; move specified types only; do not move functions unless necessary; update all imports and ensure no circular dependencies.",
    "For U6: Modify removal functions to remove error return when value does not exist; change function signatures (e.g., RemoveXxx() instead of RemoveXxx() error) if appropriate; document new behavior in GoDoc.",
    "For U7: Remove listed unnecessary examples; rename Example_xxx functions to describe purpose (e.g., Example_systemChannel -> Example_textExample); create new targeted examples (e.g., Example_ACLs); remove Output validation lines; adjust code blocks to avoid horizontal scroll.",
    "For U8: Design CLI as separate binary using cobra or similar; implement commands for genesis block, create channel transaction, and config updates; support flags/subcommands for all updatable config properties; provide comprehensive help/manual."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The existing codebase is written in Go (Hyperledger Fabric configtx package) and is already compilable and tested.",
    "All development will be done by a single developer with expert-level knowledge of Go and Hyperledger Fabric.",
    "Each activity includes necessary modifications to source code, unit tests, and GoDoc updates as per acceptance criteria.",
    "No additional refactoring beyond the specified requirements is needed; existing tests will be updated to match new signatures and behavior.",
    "The CLI tool will be built using standard Go libraries (e.g., flag or cobra) and will not require deployment or packaging beyond compilation.",
    "Effort estimates are based on typical work hours (8-hour day) and assume no interruptions or impediments."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Rename Add/Update to Set and implement override behavior",
      "activity_description": "Rename all AddXXX and UpdateXXX functions to SetXXX; modify logic to replace values instead of erroring on duplicates; for slices (e.g., AnchorPeers), ensure no duplicate is added if an equivalent exists; update all callers, examples, and GoDoc.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Rename Base() and Updated() functions",
      "activity_description": "Rename Base() to BaseConfig() and Updated() to UpdatedConfig(); update all references, examples, and GoDoc.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Implement chaining API with intermediary types",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement wrapper types (e.g., Application, Org) that expose getters/setters for chained calls; modify ConfigTx to return these types; update all relevant add/remove/set/get functions; update examples and GoDoc.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Create orderer package and move related types",
      "activity_description": "Create new package 'orderer' under configtx; move types Kafka, EtcdRaft, BatchSize, ConsensusState; update imports in all referencing files; ensure no functions are moved unless necessary; write GoDoc for the new package.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Create membership package and move MSP-related types",
      "activity_description": "Create new package 'membership' under configtx; move types SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, NodeOUs; update imports; add GoDoc for the new package.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Modify removal functions to not error on missing values",
      "activity_description": "Update all removal functions (RemoveXxx) to return nothing (or nil) if the value does not exist; adjust signatures accordingly; update logic, tests, and GoDoc to reflect new behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Clean up and reorganize GoDoc examples",
      "activity_description": "Remove the 8 listed unnecessary examples; rename Example_xxx functions to meaningful names; split large example into smaller focused examples (e.g., Example_ACLs, Example_policyRetrieval, etc.); remove Output validation lines; adjust code to avoid horizontal scroll; update GoDoc metadata as needed.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Build sample configtx CLI tool",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a command-line interface using configtx library; support commands for genesis block generation, application channel creation, and config updates with flags/subcommands for all updatable properties; include help/manual; write documentation and example usage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 140
  }
}

